 "notes": [
  "The battle replay (client/scenes/battle/battle_replay.gd), on art/reference/battle.png. Rects are the painting's, measured by flood-filling each painted window from its middle.",
  "Two blocks, split at y 1010 on the painting's even navy: everything above it is the battlefield block, drawn from the top of the screen and moved down past the phone's top inset; everything marked anchor bottom is the results block, kept at the screen's foot. On a phone taller than the painting the navy between them grows.",
  "The faces are drawn in window_you / window_them, under scene_top, whose windows are keyed see-through; the HP fills are nine-patches the whole channel long, clipped at the fraction (a partial bar ends square, as painted; a full one closes on the channel's chamfer).",
  "Fortune of War: each side's roll in its own window beside the plate, the painted die before it. The callout (CRITICAL, DODGED) is set over the crossed swords, between the frames.",
  "The results board: the story in its title band, then the rows the painting gives icons to -- gold, the crown (experience), the diamond. SKIP and CONTINUE are the painting's own plates: each button's face is its cut, laid exactly over it, and whichever of the two has nothing to do is drawn darkened.",
  "Elements of kind \"rect\" are measurements the screen reads, not things drawn.",
  "Every text rect is its line's own height, centred on the painted window it was measured from (the window's rect is the rect-kind record or the note above): a label cannot be shorter than its line, so a window-tall rect set the words' top where the window's is and dropped them."
 ],
